WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.248 --> 00:00:03.415
(audience cheering)

00:00:06.343 --> 00:00:07.677
- Get it out.

00:00:07.677 --> 00:00:08.510
Get it out.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.110
I'm so excited to see y'all.

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:10.950
It was so weird.

00:00:10.950 --> 00:00:12.870
Y'all were all in my
living room last night

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.190
with me and my kids watching it.

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:16.020
It was so good.

00:00:16.020 --> 00:00:18.270
So what do you think,
we've decorated for y'all?

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.170
We did good and evil.

00:00:19.170 --> 00:00:20.925
Do you like our audience dressed up?

00:00:20.925 --> 00:00:22.041
(audience applauding)

00:00:22.041 --> 00:00:22.874
Yes?

00:00:22.874 --> 00:00:24.036
- It's so amazing.

00:00:24.036 --> 00:00:25.350
Evers and Nevers.

00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:26.820
- I know.

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:30.660
So in the movie Kerry
and Sofia Wylie are good,

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.690
and Charlize and Sophia
Anne Caruso are evil.

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.130
I'll do that with you.

00:00:35.130 --> 00:00:37.800
So were you guys more into
like princesses or witches

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:39.960
like growing up, everybody?

00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:41.370
- Ooh.

00:00:41.370 --> 00:00:42.665
- I liked both.

00:00:42.665 --> 00:00:44.070
(agreeing with each other)

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:46.470
- Isn't that kind of like
what the film is about, too?

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.240
Is that like there's room to love it all.

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:49.917
There's room to embrace

00:00:49.917 --> 00:00:52.590
the evil and the good in you, right?

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:53.700
- What's interesting is I feel like

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:55.440
I liked the princess story.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:56.970
I liked those as a kid,

00:00:56.970 --> 00:00:59.160
but I like dressing up as the witch.

00:00:59.160 --> 00:00:59.993
- Hmm.

00:00:59.993 --> 00:01:00.870
- I don't know what that means.

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:01.703
I'll talk about it later in therapy.

00:01:01.703 --> 00:01:03.240
- [Kerry] We can unpack that for days.

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:06.060
- Yeah. I've probably
been doing it for years.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.320
But anyways, so Charlize and Kerry,

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.400
the two of you,

00:01:08.400 --> 00:01:11.310
you're an elite group
of women in Hollywood.

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.990
Like people love you.

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:14.783
We love everything you do.

00:01:14.783 --> 00:01:17.490
And you do such huge
films, the both of you.

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.680
We know you so well, TV, everything.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:23.160
So what made you gravitate
towards this project?

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:26.610
- Well, I am a single
mom to two little girls,

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:27.661
seven and ten.

00:01:27.661 --> 00:01:30.483
And my repertoires quite dark.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:33.240
- [Kelly] Monster. What?

00:01:33.240 --> 00:01:34.350
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:34.350 --> 00:01:35.220
- They didn't like that?

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:37.650
- I have a feeling they'd
have to be at least 52

00:01:37.650 --> 00:01:39.058
to see any of my work.

00:01:39.058 --> 00:01:40.080
(laughing)

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:41.073
So there's a lot of mystery there.

00:01:41.073 --> 00:01:44.430
It's like, why do we see mom on a set,

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:46.290
and she's always covered in blood?

00:01:46.290 --> 00:01:48.780
So this felt like I could do something

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.850
that's a little bit of
a love letter to them.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:55.470
And they saw it with me in
Rome a couple of weeks ago.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:56.430
Oh my God.

00:01:56.430 --> 00:01:58.560
Like you know I'm gonna be 50 soon.

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:03.560
And I was like, I thought I
was jaded and dead inside.

00:02:03.780 --> 00:02:07.050
Like I wanted their approval so badly.

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:08.970
It was almost, I had to re-watch the movie

00:02:08.970 --> 00:02:10.080
'cause I barely watched it.

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.820
I was just watching their faces.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:13.410
- Yeah, their reaction. Yeah.

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:15.960
- Yeah. So I really
wanted to do something.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:18.600
I also, I really love Paul.

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:19.860
I had worked with Paul.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:22.200
I was lucky enough to work
with Paul a couple of years ago

00:02:22.200 --> 00:02:25.140
and had such a great experience with him.

00:02:25.140 --> 00:02:27.990
And then this cast and
the story was really,

00:02:27.990 --> 00:02:30.240
it was a big world and fun.

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:34.200
And we were all coming out of lockdown,

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:35.670
so I think we were just,

00:02:35.670 --> 00:02:38.910
this felt like such a gift
to be able to go and play

00:02:38.910 --> 00:02:42.330
in these costumes coming out of COVID.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.770
- Yeah. It's so cool.

00:02:43.770 --> 00:02:45.180
It is funny 'cause I have two kids too.

00:02:45.180 --> 00:02:46.470
I'm a single mom too, and it is funny.

00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:47.463
All that you do,

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.212
it's so funny what counts to them.

00:02:50.212 --> 00:02:51.045
- Yes.
- Yes.

00:02:51.045 --> 00:02:53.936
You're like, wait, I've done
like some really cool stuff.

00:02:53.936 --> 00:02:55.380
(speaking over each other)

00:02:55.380 --> 00:02:56.430
They don't care.

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.890
I know they're impressed by
the like it's, it's like,

00:02:58.890 --> 00:03:00.300
but of course they're impressed by this

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.530
and what a cool thing to be a part of.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:02.850
Like a series.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:03.683
But what about you?

00:03:03.683 --> 00:03:04.516
What about, what about your kids?

00:03:04.516 --> 00:03:05.370
Like with the film?

00:03:05.370 --> 00:03:06.420
- Same answer.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:09.390
I mean I really, I was very
much drawn to this cast.

00:03:09.390 --> 00:03:11.670
I loved having the opportunity
to work with Charlize.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:13.560
I mean I, we didn't really know each other

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.330
before we started filming.

00:03:15.330 --> 00:03:16.800
We knew of each other obviously

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:18.000
and we'd met a couple places.

00:03:18.000 --> 00:03:21.300
But, we got on set and it
was like instant chemistry

00:03:21.300 --> 00:03:22.740
because we're both working moms

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:24.810
and because we both were
wanting to do something

00:03:24.810 --> 00:03:25.770
that our kids could watch.

00:03:25.770 --> 00:03:27.210
My kids are not watching "Scandal."

00:03:27.210 --> 00:03:28.080
- What?

00:03:28.080 --> 00:03:29.374
They don't wanna know about the white hat?

00:03:29.374 --> 00:03:30.240
- No

00:03:30.240 --> 00:03:31.500
Not yet.

00:03:31.500 --> 00:03:33.362
So it was really so wonderful to-

00:03:33.362 --> 00:03:34.195
- That's what you think.

00:03:34.195 --> 00:03:35.482
- Yeah, I know, I know.

00:03:35.482 --> 00:03:36.867
(Kelly laughing)

00:03:36.867 --> 00:03:39.360
But it was great to kind of drop in,

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.090
and also I feel like everybody

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:43.530
really made each other better.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:45.420
Like we all loved this project

00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:46.830
and loved this opportunity so much

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.000
that we were able to play.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.130
Like really play on set.

00:03:50.130 --> 00:03:52.710
- I love any time like parents and kids,

00:03:52.710 --> 00:03:54.330
a whole family can sit down

00:03:54.330 --> 00:03:56.760
and then a discussion happens afterwards.

00:03:56.760 --> 00:03:57.593
About it.

00:03:57.593 --> 00:03:59.220
About like good and evil
and what does that mean?

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:00.360
Like I have a six year old boy, too.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:01.740
It was just, it was really cool

00:04:01.740 --> 00:04:04.500
like how it kind of motivates
different conversations

00:04:04.500 --> 00:04:06.540
that you didn't really
think were gonna happen

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:07.373
with your kids.

00:04:07.373 --> 00:04:08.340
- But without hitting
you over the head, right.

00:04:08.340 --> 00:04:09.870
Like you don't feel like you're in school.

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.400
You don't feel like you're
being taught anything,

00:04:11.400 --> 00:04:13.140
but it does make you think

00:04:13.140 --> 00:04:15.030
about things we should
all be thinking about.

00:04:15.030 --> 00:04:15.863
- Yeah.

00:04:15.863 --> 00:04:17.340
Sofia, so you started acting

00:04:17.340 --> 00:04:19.200
when you were really young, right?

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:22.470
Sorry Wylie, both of
you did, but Wylie, yes.

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:25.500
So were you into it
like right off the bat?

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:26.333
- Yeah.

00:04:26.333 --> 00:04:28.260
I didn't actually start
acting professionally

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.690
until I was around 11 or 12 years old.

00:04:30.690 --> 00:04:31.860
- Well that's young.

00:04:31.860 --> 00:04:34.560
Where I'm from, that's young.

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:35.393
- That's the crazy thing.

00:04:35.393 --> 00:04:37.590
I always felt like I was so behind

00:04:37.590 --> 00:04:39.720
because all of the other
kids I was working with

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.910
had been doing it since they were infants.

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:44.280
So I was like, oh I have
to like step up my game

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.200
and like really catch up.

00:04:46.200 --> 00:04:49.080
But I always had such a
passion for performing,

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:51.300
and I had this big imagination.

00:04:51.300 --> 00:04:55.020
I grew up with like this
alter ego named Berna

00:04:55.020 --> 00:04:59.850
who had fire powers and had a
pink bob wig and cop glasses.

00:04:59.850 --> 00:05:01.860
And I just was always performing

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.330
even if no one was watching me.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:06.810
So I think this is definitely
something I was always

00:05:06.810 --> 00:05:09.030
passionate about even before
I really knew what it was.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:09.863
- You're creative kid.

00:05:09.863 --> 00:05:11.572
That's awesome, yeah.

00:05:11.572 --> 00:05:14.580
Well Sofia isn't the only one who was,

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:15.660
I love this video,

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:17.190
entertaining when she was young.

00:05:17.190 --> 00:05:20.580
Here's Sophia Anne Caruso getting
ready to perform as a kid.

00:05:20.580 --> 00:05:23.610
Listen to what happens after
her dad introduces her.

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:25.080
- Ladies and gentlemen,

00:05:25.080 --> 00:05:27.390
I would like to introduce to you

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.673
Sophia Caruso.

00:05:31.860 --> 00:05:35.970
Now Sophia will be singing
"God Bless America."

00:05:35.970 --> 00:05:37.270
- And now I won't.

00:05:38.201 --> 00:05:40.451
(cheering)

00:05:45.630 --> 00:05:47.580
- I love at a young age you were like

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.830
I will do it when I want to.

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:52.680
I feel like it reminded
me so much of my daughter.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:55.800
I was like when she was
like, not on your time sir.

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:56.940
I love, I love that.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:59.610
Were you always like, did you
always kind of know yourself

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:00.450
like that when you were a kid?

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:01.860
Like when you wanted to do
something, when you didn't?

00:06:01.860 --> 00:06:02.693
- Super rebellious.

00:06:02.693 --> 00:06:04.980
As soon as somebody
tells me to do something,

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:06.150
I do the opposite.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:06.983
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:06:06.983 --> 00:06:07.816
- Ever since I was little.

00:06:07.816 --> 00:06:08.649
- Reverse psychology.

00:06:08.649 --> 00:06:10.860
Your parents must know
this trick well, okay.

00:06:10.860 --> 00:06:12.043
- Yes, yes, they do.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:14.760
Yeah. As you can see in that video.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:15.840
And also with my character too.

00:06:15.840 --> 00:06:17.337
She's kind of like that, like

00:06:17.337 --> 00:06:19.950
she's the good girl and then
she's suddenly the bad girl.

00:06:19.950 --> 00:06:21.360
She like goes against the grain.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:22.920
- I love what you just
did with your shoulders

00:06:22.920 --> 00:06:24.360
'cause like you walking through

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:25.560
like on the little sneak peek we did.

00:06:25.560 --> 00:06:27.900
I was like, okay, music video.

00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:28.860
Like she is ready.

00:06:28.860 --> 00:06:29.693
I was like that was, it was so cool.

00:06:29.693 --> 00:06:31.440
- When it gets to slowmo.

00:06:31.440 --> 00:06:32.273
- Yes.

00:06:32.273 --> 00:06:33.240
- So badass.

00:06:33.240 --> 00:06:34.230
- Yeah.

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:36.090
Charlize, for those who
don't know the story

00:06:36.090 --> 00:06:37.500
why don't you explain like the movie.

00:06:37.500 --> 00:06:38.850
What's the premise for everybody?

00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:39.683
- Oh wow.

00:06:39.683 --> 00:06:42.960
Well the simple concept
is that there's a school

00:06:42.960 --> 00:06:45.180
for good and a school for evil.

00:06:45.180 --> 00:06:46.126
- [Kelly] You don't say.

00:06:46.126 --> 00:06:48.660
(laughing)

00:06:48.660 --> 00:06:51.330
- And we happen to be
the deans of each school.

00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:54.930
I'm the dean of the school for evil.

00:06:54.930 --> 00:06:55.890
What a shock.

00:06:55.890 --> 00:06:58.843
Like my oldest daughter was like,

00:06:58.843 --> 00:07:02.583
oh Mom, ugh again.

00:07:03.870 --> 00:07:05.970
The only movie they've ever
seen like a little bit of

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:08.160
was when I played the
Evil Queen in Snow White.

00:07:08.160 --> 00:07:12.093
And she's like, ugh, can
you only do that part?

00:07:13.094 --> 00:07:16.230
She's like, can't you
like do a different part?

00:07:16.230 --> 00:07:17.220
I was like, oh my god.

00:07:17.220 --> 00:07:19.623
My children are like,
just wear a dress, please.

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:21.600
- It is different though.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:23.160
It's so funny, 'cause
whenever I found out you were,

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:24.420
I was like, they're different.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:27.000
Even how you, it's like, it's almost like

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:28.680
even how you introduce
yourself at one part

00:07:28.680 --> 00:07:30.600
in your, your, everything is different.

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:32.280
Your mannerisms, it's interesting.

00:07:32.280 --> 00:07:33.624
- There's a lot of ways to be evil.

00:07:33.624 --> 00:07:34.740
- Yeah.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:35.573
- But anyway-

00:07:35.573 --> 00:07:36.960
- And she seems to find them all.

00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:40.380
- These two young ladies get dropped

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:43.230
in what they think is the wrong school.

00:07:43.230 --> 00:07:45.430
Just to find out that

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:48.030
maybe how they see themselves

00:07:48.030 --> 00:07:49.920
are not actually their authentic selves.

00:07:49.920 --> 00:07:54.540
And it's the discovery that you
can't just be all one thing.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:57.300
And so we are all a
little bit of everything,

00:07:57.300 --> 00:08:00.243
and so we saved the day.

00:08:02.040 --> 00:08:03.610
- They had nothing to do with it.

00:08:03.610 --> 00:08:05.430
(laughing)

00:08:05.430 --> 00:08:06.442
- All about us.

00:08:06.442 --> 00:08:07.821
(laughing)

00:08:07.821 --> 00:08:10.320
- Yeah, you really killed
it there at the end.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:11.760
And I remember what happens.

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:12.593
I was like, yes.

00:08:12.593 --> 00:08:13.426
- The COVID hug.

00:08:13.426 --> 00:08:15.034
- Yeah, it was good, it was good.

00:08:15.034 --> 00:08:17.970
(laughing) I just remembered the, yes.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.500
I was talking about something else,

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.514
but I just remembered like, oh good.

00:08:21.514 --> 00:08:23.130
Yeah, it was really good.

00:08:23.130 --> 00:08:24.090
Oh my god, I love it.

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:26.640
So Sophia and Sofia's
characters are friends

00:08:26.640 --> 00:08:28.800
who are set up to be enemies.

00:08:28.800 --> 00:08:31.830
How do you think the dynamic
of that kind of plays out

00:08:31.830 --> 00:08:33.120
in real world as well?

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:37.590
'Cause I felt like, I
don't, and maybe it's just

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:38.423
in the musician world.

00:08:38.423 --> 00:08:40.200
I don't know if it's the
same in the acting world.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.290
But they always try and pit
females against each other.

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:45.420
They do in the music world at least.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.100
And I thought that was
kind of interesting.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.840
- It's funny, yesterday
we were doing an interview

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:49.860
and somebody said,

00:08:49.860 --> 00:08:51.540
you guys have such great
chemistry up there.

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:52.980
Did it feel competitive?

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.180
And we were like, what?

00:08:54.180 --> 00:08:57.450
Like no, it felt so inspiring.

00:08:57.450 --> 00:08:58.470
I think was the word you used.

00:08:58.470 --> 00:08:59.303
Like which was so great.

00:08:59.303 --> 00:09:03.090
It was, it was, we kept
upping the ante for each other

00:09:03.090 --> 00:09:05.160
and encouraging each other to play

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:07.050
and find new ways to do the scene.

00:09:07.050 --> 00:09:09.960
It didn't, it didn't
feel competitive at all.

00:09:09.960 --> 00:09:13.710
- There's just been so little
opportunity for us, right.

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:16.170
And so the little that did come around,

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:18.270
instead of acknowledging
that there was a need

00:09:18.270 --> 00:09:20.100
for more opportunity,

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:23.340
they made it about women
not supporting each other.

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.560
And I think it was the easy way out

00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:28.990
because I have never been more supported

00:09:29.910 --> 00:09:31.710
than by the women in my life.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.543
Inspired by the women of my life.

00:09:34.560 --> 00:09:36.870
Been brave because of
the women in my life.

00:09:36.870 --> 00:09:38.670
So we just need more opportunity.

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:39.870
We need.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:41.960
That's why I love being
in this film because...

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:44.960
(audience cheering)

00:09:47.240 --> 00:09:49.890
Just being a part of something
that can create opportunity

00:09:49.890 --> 00:09:51.540
for like these two young ladies.

00:09:51.540 --> 00:09:55.189
To see them in this film,
makes my old dead heart feel...

00:09:55.189 --> 00:09:57.330
(laughing)

00:09:57.330 --> 00:09:58.163
We need more of that.

00:09:58.163 --> 00:09:58.996
We need more of that.

00:09:58.996 --> 00:10:01.110
- This is their film, you
know, the two of them.

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:04.350
And for us to be able to
support them in these roles

00:10:04.350 --> 00:10:08.010
where we're really just really amplifying

00:10:08.010 --> 00:10:09.480
their incredible talent.

00:10:09.480 --> 00:10:10.920
They carry this movie,

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.830
and we're so proud to be
a part of something that

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:15.990
shines a light on them and
all of the young people

00:10:15.990 --> 00:10:16.823
in that film.

00:10:16.823 --> 00:10:17.656
(audience cheering)

00:10:17.656 --> 00:10:19.287
And what I really wanted to touch on too

00:10:19.287 --> 00:10:21.240
is, I thought it was cool, like sometimes

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:23.460
you see like females
taking over, you know,

00:10:23.460 --> 00:10:26.730
characters from books that
were males originally.

00:10:26.730 --> 00:10:29.970
And I love that the book
originally has all this

00:10:29.970 --> 00:10:31.320
like female empowerment in it.

00:10:31.320 --> 00:10:32.280
There's plenty of roles.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:33.113
There's males too, but I just-

00:10:33.113 --> 00:10:34.029
- The guys are great.

00:10:34.029 --> 00:10:34.862
They're always great.

00:10:34.862 --> 00:10:35.695
- They are, they're great.

00:10:35.695 --> 00:10:36.780
But I just meant, I found it interesting.

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.100
It wasn't like they had to go in and go,

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:40.650
oh we're gonna recast this as
a female to be more inclusive.

00:10:40.650 --> 00:10:42.900
It was like, it was already inclusive.

00:10:42.900 --> 00:10:44.730
And I found that really cool.

00:10:44.730 --> 00:10:47.370
- One of the coolest
moments of my career so far

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:49.080
was after we shot one of the big scenes

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:51.450
where we're like introducing
the rules of the school.

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:53.280
And in a break, Lawrence Fishburne,

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:55.470
who's one of the cool guys in the film,

00:10:55.470 --> 00:10:58.290
he comes walking across
the hall, and he said

00:10:58.290 --> 00:11:01.530
watching you and Charlize
up there was so much fun.

00:11:01.530 --> 00:11:03.450
That's why I did this movie.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:07.309
(speaking over each other)

00:11:07.309 --> 00:11:09.390
- Was it like intimidating at all?

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:10.223
Like to work with him?

00:11:10.223 --> 00:11:11.160
Or just inspiring?

00:11:11.160 --> 00:11:12.543
Was it, was it cool?

00:11:12.543 --> 00:11:14.431
(laughing) Tell me more.

00:11:14.431 --> 00:11:17.550
(laughing) I'm just curious.

00:11:17.550 --> 00:11:18.870
- I don't think I was intimidated.

00:11:18.870 --> 00:11:21.070
I didn't really have
time to be intimidated.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:23.070
And there's always something to learn.

00:11:23.070 --> 00:11:25.560
Whether your co-star
is famous or not famous

00:11:25.560 --> 00:11:27.480
or legend or not.

00:11:27.480 --> 00:11:29.010
I think there's always
something to be learned.

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:29.843
- How about you?

00:11:29.843 --> 00:11:30.676
How did you feel?

00:11:30.676 --> 00:11:31.860
- I was the exact opposite.

00:11:31.860 --> 00:11:34.230
I was like freaking out.

00:11:34.230 --> 00:11:35.250
I mean, look at them.

00:11:35.250 --> 00:11:38.290
Like I've grown up
watching the both of you.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:39.123
- I'm not that old.

00:11:39.123 --> 00:11:41.749
(laughing)

00:11:41.749 --> 00:11:42.930
- Like from a few years ago.

00:11:42.930 --> 00:11:43.763
- Exactly.

00:11:44.850 --> 00:11:47.160
And I tried to play it so cool.

00:11:47.160 --> 00:11:48.753
I was like, hey Kerry, was up.

00:11:50.277 --> 00:11:52.347
Like casual, yeah.

00:11:52.347 --> 00:11:54.480
But inside I'm like literally shaking,

00:11:54.480 --> 00:11:56.760
and I just remember like
the first day on set

00:11:56.760 --> 00:11:58.620
I had with you Kerry,

00:11:58.620 --> 00:12:01.440
you touched my face in one of the takes.

00:12:01.440 --> 00:12:03.090
And I literally went to
my parents and I was like,

00:12:03.090 --> 00:12:04.997
I'm never washing my face again.

00:12:04.997 --> 00:12:07.247
(laughing)

00:12:08.459 --> 00:12:11.469
- I love that. I love that.

00:12:11.469 --> 00:12:12.302
Welcome back.

00:12:12.302 --> 00:12:15.157
We're here with Kerry
Washington, Charlize Theron,

00:12:15.157 --> 00:12:17.687
Sophia Anne Caruso and Sofia Wylie.

00:12:17.687 --> 00:12:18.520
(audience cheering)

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:20.647
So together they star in
the new Netflix movie,

00:12:20.647 --> 00:12:23.940
"The School for Good and
Evil," which is streaming now.

00:12:23.940 --> 00:12:26.850
Everyone in our audience
also has chosen a side.

00:12:26.850 --> 00:12:28.243
Good or evil.

00:12:28.243 --> 00:12:29.550
(audience cheering)

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:32.400
Okay. So you're both
in the school of evil.

00:12:32.400 --> 00:12:34.230
So what's one bad thing you've done

00:12:34.230 --> 00:12:36.240
that you've gotten away with?

00:12:36.240 --> 00:12:39.450
Ooh, fess up on national TV.

00:12:39.450 --> 00:12:40.560
No pressure.

00:12:40.560 --> 00:12:43.320
- I mean, well the other
day I did steal some limes

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.490
from a restaurant.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:46.200
- Wait, is that stealing?

00:12:46.200 --> 00:12:47.106
Am I?

00:12:47.106 --> 00:12:49.080
(Charlize laughing)

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:50.130
- Are you more evil than you knew?

00:12:50.130 --> 00:12:50.963
- Wait, is that stealing?

00:12:50.963 --> 00:12:52.320
I feel like they put them
out there for you to take.

00:12:52.320 --> 00:12:55.080
- No, no there were like
lime trees in the restaurant

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:57.180
with real limes, and I
took like four of them.

00:12:57.180 --> 00:12:58.650
Just like shoved 'em in my pocket.

00:12:58.650 --> 00:12:59.580
- That would be stealing

00:12:59.580 --> 00:13:00.413
- [Kelly] That would be stealing.

00:13:00.413 --> 00:13:02.343
- That would be stealing.

00:13:02.343 --> 00:13:03.870
- It's like half stealing.

00:13:03.870 --> 00:13:05.670
They put it out there.

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:07.320
You're coming there to
consume their products.

00:13:07.320 --> 00:13:08.153
- It's a tree.

00:13:08.153 --> 00:13:08.986
- It's a product.

00:13:08.986 --> 00:13:11.190
You might be able to justify that one.

00:13:11.190 --> 00:13:12.230
Kind of steal, stealing.

00:13:12.230 --> 00:13:14.299
(audience clapping)

00:13:14.299 --> 00:13:15.132
- It's just a lime.

00:13:15.132 --> 00:13:18.270
- Watch out for her in your
restaurants, everybody.

00:13:18.270 --> 00:13:20.480
What about you? What have you done?

00:13:20.480 --> 00:13:22.800
- I, well I don't know
if I get away with it,

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:27.673
but I have maybe more than on one occasion

00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:30.840
gone to take pizza at a kids' party

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:32.280
before the kids got fed.

00:13:32.280 --> 00:13:34.800
Claiming that I was getting it for my kid.

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:35.880
- Oh.

00:13:35.880 --> 00:13:39.302
I 100%, I did that the last
birthday I just did with my son.

00:13:39.302 --> 00:13:40.404
- Okay, okay, good.

00:13:40.404 --> 00:13:41.389
(speaking over each other)

00:13:41.389 --> 00:13:43.470
- And part of me is like, why
don't I just say it's for me.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:45.810
But then I feel bad because
it is like before our all the,

00:13:45.810 --> 00:13:47.610
the kids just get so into the party

00:13:47.610 --> 00:13:50.910
that I'm like this beautiful
hot pizza is going to waste.

00:13:50.910 --> 00:13:51.743
- I know.

00:13:51.743 --> 00:13:52.590
And they let it get cold while they're

00:13:52.590 --> 00:13:53.474
jumping on the trampoline.

00:13:53.474 --> 00:13:54.307
- Yeah, exactly, they don't care.

00:13:54.307 --> 00:13:55.500
(speaking over each other)

00:13:55.500 --> 00:13:58.413
And I'm like, the cheese
is like nice and hot still.

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:00.570
- So what about you?

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.040
Even though you're school of good,

00:14:02.040 --> 00:14:04.230
have y'all ever done anything
that you've gotten away with?

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:06.124
Oh, I thought we were
gonna get a good question.

00:14:06.124 --> 00:14:07.154
(laughing)

00:14:07.154 --> 00:14:08.970
(speaking over each other)

00:14:08.970 --> 00:14:10.080
- No, that's boring.

00:14:10.080 --> 00:14:11.244
- Yeah this is, okay.

00:14:11.244 --> 00:14:13.331
(laughing)

00:14:13.331 --> 00:14:14.164
What about you?

00:14:14.164 --> 00:14:16.350
What have you done that
you've gotten away with.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:20.430
- I was just an odd
kid and so I, you know,

00:14:20.430 --> 00:14:23.580
they do this weird thing
with girls' outfits.

00:14:23.580 --> 00:14:25.140
They don't give you pockets.

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:28.500
And so I loved collecting
things, collecting rocks,

00:14:28.500 --> 00:14:31.039
like anything that I
found pretty or sparkly.

00:14:31.039 --> 00:14:34.148
- Collecting, stealing,
collecting, stealing.

00:14:34.148 --> 00:14:35.639
(laughing)

00:14:35.639 --> 00:14:36.603
- Exactly.

00:14:37.500 --> 00:14:39.990
And I think it was
around like from the age

00:14:39.990 --> 00:14:43.200
of like three to five.

00:14:43.200 --> 00:14:44.820
I'm like three to seventeen.

00:14:44.820 --> 00:14:47.490
No, three to five, I would collect rocks,

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:50.948
and I would just shove them in my pants.

00:14:50.948 --> 00:14:53.819
(speaking over each other)

00:14:53.819 --> 00:14:55.387
- I'm taking from the earth.

00:14:55.387 --> 00:14:57.000
(speaking over each other)

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:57.930
- Virginia Wolf.

00:14:57.930 --> 00:14:59.040
Sorry, wrong person.

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.240
Sorry.

00:15:00.240 --> 00:15:01.920
- So that's the most
evil thing you've done

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:03.261
and got away with?

00:15:03.261 --> 00:15:05.070
(speaking over each other)

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.983
That's certainly not the
most evil thing I've done.

00:15:06.983 --> 00:15:07.920
(laughing)

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:09.183
It's just what I chose to say.

00:15:09.183 --> 00:15:11.820
(laughing)

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:12.653
- What about you?

00:15:12.653 --> 00:15:13.860
You're not getting off the hook.

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:14.774
You're not getting-

00:15:14.774 --> 00:15:16.251
- I feel like we need to
break for a commercial.

00:15:16.251 --> 00:15:18.180
(laughing)

00:15:18.180 --> 00:15:19.013
I don't know.

00:15:19.013 --> 00:15:22.530
I mean, I feel like the,
I was mostly a good girl.

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:24.840
The evil things, I don't
wanna admit on television.

00:15:24.840 --> 00:15:25.673
- Amen.

00:15:26.670 --> 00:15:31.200
- You know what I, when I was
little, I used to lie a lot.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.192
And then I found acting.

00:15:33.192 --> 00:15:36.390
Because I had like such an imagination,

00:15:36.390 --> 00:15:38.460
and I would just make up stories

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:40.890
about like what my family
did over the weekend.

00:15:40.890 --> 00:15:42.390
And my teachers would be
like, it's so interesting.

00:15:42.390 --> 00:15:44.850
And my mother would be
like, that never happened.

00:15:44.850 --> 00:15:47.100
But then I realized I
could use my imagination

00:15:47.100 --> 00:15:49.081
in ways that wasn't evil and hurtful.

00:15:49.081 --> 00:15:51.990
- Way to take a negative and
make a positive out of it.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:52.823
Nicely done.

00:15:52.823 --> 00:15:53.656
(audience clapping)

00:15:53.656 --> 00:15:54.990
A professional liar.

00:15:54.990 --> 00:15:55.890
You get paid for it now.

00:15:55.890 --> 00:15:56.723
- Yeah, exactly.

00:15:56.723 --> 00:15:58.121
- That was just your pregame.

00:15:58.121 --> 00:15:59.202
I like it.

00:15:59.202 --> 00:16:00.196
- Yeah. I like it.

